MID_SE_Kai_Led_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Kai_Led_B_001: If it isn't Cai! Found love lately?
MID_SE_Kai_Led_B_002: Really? You're just gonna hit me with that outta\nthe blue?
MID_SE_Kai_Led_B_003: I just remember that during the Heroic Games,\nyou said you didn't know much about it.
MID_SE_Kai_Led_B_004: Now you're an eligible young man, so I thought I'd\nfollow up and ask.
MID_SE_Kai_Led_B_005: Come on! There must be one or two flings you can\ntell me about, surely.
MID_SE_Kai_Led_B_006: Same old Leda. You haven't changed a bit.
MID_SE_Kai_Led_B_007: You know you don't have to hide behind that\ncheerful mask with me, right?
MID_SE_Kai_Led_B_008: Ah...
MID_SE_Kai_Led_B_009: I've been curious about it since we first met, the way\nyou keep your desire for revenge behind your smile.
MID_SE_Kai_Led_B_010: You still hate Bertrand, don't you?
MID_SE_Kai_Led_B_011: Bertrand's gone, but that doesn't mean your hatred\nfor him has disappeared, right? 
MID_SE_Kai_Led_B_012: You're that worried about me, huh? You really are a\ngood guy.
MID_SE_Kai_Led_B_013: But actually, you don't have me quite right—I'm not\nfaking it as much as you might think.
MID_SE_Kai_Led_B_014: Since I was a little girl, I've been cheerful by nature.\nTo the point that I was a little bit unruly.
MID_SE_Kai_Led_B_015: My mother used to say that the room lit up when I\nwas in it.
MID_SE_Kai_Led_B_016: And my father... I can still remember how he used\nto beam at me. I loved making the two of them smile.
MID_SE_Kai_Led_B_017: So you had that experience too. "Loved by your\nparents," and all that.
MID_SE_Kai_Led_B_018: Hehe. Alright, I see what you're doing. Turning my\nown words back at me?
MID_SE_Kai_Led_B_019: But you're right, that's how it felt. And that's why\nI grieved my old life so bitterly.
MID_SE_Kai_Led_B_020: I thought of us as opposites. Me trying to kill the man\nwho killed my father, you trying to keep yours alive.
MID_SE_Kai_Led_B_021: But, even though our goals were incompatible,\nmaybe we were the same at heart.
MID_SE_Kai_Led_B_022: All we wanted was a happy life with our parents.\nThe difference was just—you could get yours back.
MID_SE_Kai_Led_B_023: I guess you're right. But now Pop's gone too.
MID_SE_Kai_Led_B_024: Oh, Cai. I'm sorry—for saying I hated you.
MID_SE_Kai_Led_B_025: I know it won't make up for being so cruel, but would\nyou tell me about your father?
MID_SE_Kai_Led_B_026: Of course. And I want to hear more about your\nparents too.
MID_SE_Kai_Led_B_027: I have a feeling there's a lot to tell.
MID_SE_Kai_Led_B_028: Oh, you have no idea! I mean, I've never seen a\nlove like theirs. They were so well matched...
MID_SE_Kai_Led_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Kai_Led_A_001: So Aurora kept herself to the temple? Then she must\nhave... Wow, she must have hardly seen anyone.
MID_SE_Kai_Led_A_002: Yeah, and Pop was a real tough guy. It's a wonder\nthe two of them ever got together.
MID_SE_Kai_Led_A_003: Well, if love is one thing, it's irrational. You never\nknow where it'll take you.
MID_SE_Kai_Led_A_004: My father was the viceroy—a serious, sturdy man,\nwho kept himself to careful routines.
MID_SE_Kai_Led_A_005: Around my mother though! The man changed\ncompletely, turned blustery and blundering.
MID_SE_Kai_Led_A_006: Hehehe. I guess he really fell for your mom.
MID_SE_Kai_Led_A_007: You and I, we're the products of our parents' passion\nfor each other. Doesn't that make you feel proud?
MID_SE_Kai_Led_A_008: Though of course, passion can go in the other\ndirection—make you want to destroy everything.
MID_SE_Kai_Led_A_009: You mean like your vendetta?
MID_SE_Kai_Led_A_010: I still say obsessing over vengeance is a bad idea.
MID_SE_Kai_Led_A_011: Obsessing over vengeance? You'd write off my whole\nlife just like that?
MID_SE_Kai_Led_A_012: The thought must have occurred to you before\ntoo, right?
MID_SE_Kai_Led_A_013: The idea that you could live a better life if you\nweren't fixated on revenge?
MID_SE_Kai_Led_A_014: I'm not saying you should ignore what happened to\nyou. I just want you to be happy.
MID_SE_Kai_Led_A_015: Cai. You may look grown up.
MID_SE_Kai_Led_A_016: But on the inside, it seems you haven't changed\nmuch. You're still green.
MID_SE_Kai_Led_A_017: That's a little harsh. Maybe I haven't changed much,\nbut have you?
MID_SE_Kai_Led_A_018: And if you haven't, does that mean you still hate me?
MID_SE_Kai_Led_A_019: That's— Of course I didn't mean that. Don't put\nwords in my mouth.
MID_SE_Kai_Led_A_020: I think it's sweet that after all this time, you're the\nsame kindhearted Cai as ever.
MID_SE_Kai_Led_A_021: The kind of person who makes me feel safer when\nthey're by my side.
MID_SE_Kai_Led_A_022: R-really? Well...I, um, uh...
MID_SE_Kai_Led_A_023: Well...I'd better keep an eye on you, then.
MID_SE_Kai_Led_A_024: I guess...you're the answer to any questions about\nmy love life.
MID_SE_Kai_Led_A_025: Haha! Let's not get ahead of ourselves.